        <article class="lesson-article">
            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 11</span><h1>Prototype Pattern</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>20 min</span><span class="lesson-level advanced">Advanced</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Intent</h2>
                    <p>Create new objects by cloning existing ones, avoiding costly creation from scratch.</p>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>ICloneable Interface</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public class Document : ICloneable
{
    public string Title { get; set; }
    public string Content { get; set; }
    public List&lt;string&gt; Tags { get; set; } = new();

    public object Clone()
    {
        // Shallow copy
        return MemberwiseClone();
    }
}

var original = new Document { Title = "Report", Content = "..." };
var copy = (Document)original.Clone();</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Deep Clone</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public class Document : ICloneable
{
    public string Title { get; set; }
    public string Content { get; set; }
    public List&lt;string&gt; Tags { get; set; } = new();

    public object Clone()
    {
        // Deep copy - clone reference types too
        var clone = (Document)MemberwiseClone();
        clone.Tags = new List&lt;string&gt;(Tags);  // New list with same items
        return clone;
    }
}

// Using JSON serialization for deep clone
public T DeepClone&lt;T&gt;(T obj)
{
    var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(obj);
    return JsonSerializer.Deserialize&lt;T&gt;(json)!;
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Record Types (C# 9+)</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Records have built-in with-expressions for cloning
public record Person(string Name, int Age, Address Address);
public record Address(string City, string Country);

var original = new Person("John", 30, new Address("London", "UK"));

// Clone with modifications
var clone = original with { Name = "Jane" };
var moved = original with { Address = original.Address with { City = "Paris" } };</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                        <LessonTakeaway>Prototype creates new objects by copying existing ones.</LessonTakeaway>
                        <LessonTakeaway>Shallow copy shares references; deep copy creates new ones.</LessonTakeaway>
                        <LessonTakeaway>C# records provide built-in clone-with-modification.</LessonTakeaway>
                    </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
